    "created_at": "2016-05-15T17:18:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-15T17:18:52Z",
    "body": "I don't know of any analogy in a library. This API would need all of the arguments that `addEventListener` needs since it's potentially calling both add and remove. The analogy to `classList` isn't good because 1) that case is just toggling a simple string, there is no other associated state, and 2) unlike `classList.contains()`, there is no method exposed to determine whether any event listener is currently attached at all, much less attached with a specific handler and set of event options.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
